{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/435774-abyssal-redemption","id":435774,"title":"Abyssal Redemption","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Abyssal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-10T09:06:59-07:00","id":435774,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon1.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Abyssal Redemption","content":"Hi All,<br /> <br /> I'm sure there is a thread somewhere buried with this very topic, but I was wondering if I could probe the collective Exalted conscious on &quot;official&quot; and creative ways to redeem/turn an Abyssal back to their Solar nature. I've read that the best way is presenting the Abyssal to the Unconquered Sun, which unfortunately is impossible in my current campaign as Yu Shan is completely cut off from the realm. To give some back story, I played a Twilight caste for close to five years, and while on a mission to treaty with the Mask of Winters, at Juggernaut, I fell under the influence of a demon, and I decided to pledge myself to the Mask of Winters... My new PC, a reimagined version of Pai Mei (Shaw Brothers, and recently Kill Bill) is on a mission to find the Abyssal and turn him back, as the Scarlet Empress has returned and is causing all sorts of trouble with the defense grid.<br /> <br /> I've found the Abyssal, who has dethroned the Mask of Winters, and is now a Deathlord... This is from my Storyteller:<br /> <br /> <i>Pai Sheng has tracked down rumors of the Abysal Devon Hida, and as was suspected, all signs point to Juggernaut, the living fortress of Devon\u2019s creator the Mask of Winters. It seems that what Mask told your compatriot may be true: Devon has risen in power and may have in fact usurped the Deathlord. Pai Sheng crests a hill, expecting to see the hulking Juggernaut in the distance, but all that is left are the ruins of Thorns. Pai Sheng approaches the ruined city. An enormous crater sits where Juggernaut used to be. From the shadows, the pale shades of ghosts look on with suspicion. \u201cIf it is the Mask of Winters you seek,\u201d one says, \u201cthen you are too late, Lawgiver. He fled upon word of the Scarlet Empress\u2019s return.\u201d Pai Sheng readies a reply, but before he can speak a voice behind him says, \u201cI believe I am the one you are looking for.\u201d Standing atop a pile of ash is an imposing figure, black holes in place of eyes, burnt flesh uncovered by any clothing save a simple loincloth, and clicking skeletal hands. \u201cYou've asked for Devon Hida. I gave up that name the day I was turned. I am Flame of Fallen Hope.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> I super appreciate your thoughts!<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Magma Kraken EVERYTHING!!!&quot; - A response fitting for any situation","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/162-mr_bony_hands","name":"Mr_Bony_Hands","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T10:11:12-07:00","id":435877,"title":"","content":"You may find some of what you seek in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/407624-redemption-3rd-edition\">here</a>. I recall there was also some guidance somewhere in the Scroll of Errata, or lying in the Ink Monkeys Compendium, so I would seek those out as well, if you're curious.<br /> <br /> The long and short of it is that it's not an easy thing to do. It may well not even be known as a possibility in-setting, nor exist as more than a rumor. A common thread is that the Abyssal in question needs to desire and pursue it. If it's to happen, I'd advise personalizing it to the Abyssal in question; a one-size-fits-all approach has never felt like a good fit, to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T10:24:39-07:00","id":435893,"title":"","content":"It should not surprise you that the first step, is an asswhooping. There is black essence all over his Exaltation and its up to you to slap it right off.<br /> <br /> You gotta beat this guy so hard, the Neverborn feel it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T10:37:17-07:00","id":435927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/435774-abyssal-redemption?p=435893#post435893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is black essence all over his Exaltation and its up to you to slap it right off.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ke9wtbzGjCI#t=5m50s\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;That's racist...&quot;</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T15:16:20-07:00","id":436329,"title":"","content":"I played an abyssal named Walker upon Shattered Waves. he was a westerner who ran a fleet of privateers out of Coral. His inspiration for taking the first steps down the path was a woman he fell head over heels for. He did a lot of very bad things before meeting her, but tried to right wrongs (sometimes successfully) after they met.He got the stealth charm that makes you look like a solar and also the charm that lets you learn solar charms. This was the key to unlocking his essence. after a long quest, during which his circle were sacrificed (this was heart-breaking) he finally met Sol Invictus, the god responsible for the passage of time and the god of exaltation in yushan. they froze him in time (so he wouldn't die) yanked his essence out, fixed it and stuck it back in. Yay, Solar with no great curse! (being that it must be removed for the neverborn to add the resonance track)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1044-veritas1980","name":"Veritas1980","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1044_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":4,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T06:16:43-07:00","id":438312,"title":"","content":"It has to be a personal story. It's not like you can roll a bunch of dice or perform some special ritual and be redeemed.<br /> <br /> But as someone said above, the first and most important step is that the Abyssal must sincerely <i>desire</i> redemption. It's not like you can punch the bad out of him.<br /> <br /> I'm fond of &quot;sacrificing their life in a heroic fashion only to rise from the brink of death a second time as a Solar&quot;, but it has to fit your story.<br /> <br /> You might also consider the possibility of failing to redeem them, of course. Sometimes that can make a good story, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T15:46:55-07:00","id":469643,"title":"","content":"Hi Everyone,<br /> <br /> Thanks so much for all of he great ideas! Unfortunately, I didn't manage to convert the Abyssal, but swayed him to help... at least I thought I did. Last minute, he betrayed us, and brought forth his true mentor... The Mask of Winters, who laid waste to our party after 6 years of sessions. However, the GM used this as an opportunity to bring us to the upcoming 3E Campaign he is planning (from a story perspective). The setting will be that Creation has been turned into a vast Shadowland, and our newly created Exalted will attempt to travel back in time to stop of the Mask of Winters's take over the Imperial Manse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Magma Kraken EVERYTHING!!!&quot; - A response fitting for any situation","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/162-mr_bony_hands","name":"Mr_Bony_Hands","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T16:05:59-07:00","id":469648,"title":"","content":"Sounds like a fun, epic game. I would just encourage your ST to note, when the 3e book comes out, that the scope of things have changed, and under 2e rules this may have been much easier. Still, sounds like something that would be awesome to play through.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T07:26:01-07:00","id":471202,"title":"","content":"I've handled one Abyssal redemption in a game and I basically did it all as a narrative experience.<br /> <br /> <b>Step 1:</b> Abyssal feels honest self-contempt and is attracted to Creation for honest and good reasons rather than something like out of jealousy.<br /> <b>Step 2:</b> If an Abyssal is honest enough, the Sun takes notice. He must personally bestow the redemption upon an Abyssal but he doesn't do it willy nilly. To walk in the light, you must deserve to walk in the light. If the Abyssal has potential, he may grant him/her a vision, much like when exalting a Zenith Caste.<br /> <b>Step 3:</b> The Abyssal sees the vision through, proving to Sol that he was right in putting faith in the Abyssal.<br /> <b>Step 4:</b> Sol redeems the Abyssal.<br /> <br /> For the sake of my Abyssal, the steps looked like this (this may or may not be a spoiler from my webcomic, so continue at your own peril if you're a reader).<br /> <br /> <b>Step 1:</b> The Abyssal had never given or experienced love, or even harbored any true feelings of affection, both in life and pseudo-death. She used to be ugly but was now beautiful -- something she had always wanted to be -- but she felt more empty than ever before. She found a friend in Creation, and she could almost imagine what it would be like to almost care about that person.<br /> <b>Step 2:</b> Sol felt her pain and longing, and he visited her in a dream, telling her that if she could find real love and find someone who could love her for real, then her life would no longer be empty.<br /> <b>Step 3:</b> She eventually met a man, grew to care for him (but it was still not love). Eventually she bore a child, and upon seeing her newborn child for the first time, she knew what Sol had told her and was, for the first time in her life, happy.<br /> <b>Step 4:</b> She redeemed.<br /> <br /> I think it would be rather cliche to go with the whole &quot;love solves all problems&quot; plot, but for the purpose of this particular character, it made sense, and I think a redemption story should be something very personal for the Abyssal who wants to be redeemed. No redemption looks the same, and even though Sol has the power to, he will not redeem Abyssals willy nilly. It's called redemption for a reason; it must be something the Abyssal does to him-/herself, perhaps with a bit of guidance, but it should be treated as a personal journey more than as a gift from up high.<br /> <br /> That's how I deal with it at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T15:39:28-07:00","id":471766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/435774-abyssal-redemption?p=435877#post435877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You may find some of what you seek in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/407624-redemption-3rd-edition\">here</a>. I recall there was also some guidance somewhere in the Scroll of Errata, or lying in the Ink Monkeys Compendium, so I would seek those out as well, if you're curious.<br /> <br /> The long and short of it is that it's not an easy thing to do. It may well not even be known as a possibility in-setting, nor exist as more than a rumor. A common thread is that the Abyssal in question needs to desire and pursue it. If it's to happen, I'd advise personalizing it to the Abyssal in question; a one-size-fits-all approach has never felt like a good fit, to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> IIRC, if an Abyssal considers the possibility, he/she will realise it's possible at the very least. The Scroll of Errata has the closest thing to rules on the subject (which mostly boil down to guidelines- one Story per dot of Essence should have the Abyssal pursuing redemption, it involved understanding the four Virtues, and it lays out what happens when the redemption actually happens). But yes, it should be a personal journey for each Abyssal. I do think it absolutely shouldn't be a journey taken on their own, however- whether it's one Abyssal who has her Lunar Mate at her side, always supporting her, or the one who gains support from the rest of a (Solar) Circle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}